    desc: "Parts Module (3).xlsx · sheet “Parts Maintenance”. Category is a banner ROW, never a field: everything under a banner belongs to it until the next one. 69 parts seeded from 22 of the 179 categories the sheet names (217 banner rows carry them) — the ones the seeded hulls actually name, in their single-valued columns (Standard Safety Gear, PFD Type, Anchor Kit, Tie Downs) and in the ten-slot P/D band at Boat Module!JT..KC. Boat Module!JT..KC resolves into THIS sheet's column C at 99.59% over all 5,918 populated cells. 1 of them sits below the OBSOLETE PARTS divider at C2918 and is marked Discontinued — kept, because a live hull still names it, and never offered. The other 2879 parts in the library are NOT here, and that is the reachability policy of FITMENT_RULES.md §5.7 rather than a sampling cap: a part no seeded hull names has nothing in this set to belong to. Selling a part off the shelf that no boat's P/D band lists is a real requirement if the dealer has it, and it is raised as one in SEED_AT_FULL_SCALE.md §6 rather than settled by a size decision.",
